Manual review corrections (first review pass), none upstream-source-specific --
these are typographic/LaTeX-quality fixes to the converter's otherwise
faithful transcription:

- Exercise 3: a sentence comma was trapped inside the closing math span
  (`$x\text{-axis,}$`), producing OpenStax's default over-wide "Relation"-
  style spacing before the comma; moved outside to `$x\text{-axis}$,`.
- Two instances of "$x\,\text{and}\,y$" (the indicated-values intro and the
  hint before exercise 35) manually glued two variables and the word "and"
  into one math span with ad-hoc `\,` spacing; unwrapped to plain prose
  "$x$ and $y$", consistent with this repo's convention of keeping English
  outside math mode.
- Exercise 21's (a)/(b) sub-list wrote "Along the x-axis"/"Along the y-axis"
  as bare prose variables, inconsistent with the parallel sub-list under
  exercise 18 in the same file, which correctly uses `$x\text{-axis}$`/
  `$y\text{-axis}$`; brought into line with that sibling exercise.
- Exercise 37's piecewise continuity definition used a non-stretchy
  `\{\begin{matrix}...\end{matrix}\}` — plain-height braces around a
  multi-line case split, with a stray unmatched trailing `\}` besides. Since
  amsmath is already loaded by exercises.cls and this repo's own convention
  for piecewise functions (see vol2-3-7-improper-integrals.tex and
  vol3-5-2-double-integrals-over-general-regions.tex) is
  `\begin{cases}...\end{cases}`, switched to that: automatic height-matched
  single left brace, left-aligned cases, no orphaned closing brace.

